# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# handOffs/delta-log.md — union merge (S354)
#
# The log is APPEND-ONLY and its entries are one-line records. Every collision
# observed has been a tail-append conflict: two concurrent sessions each append
# after the same last entry. `union` keeps BOTH sides automatically instead of
# raising a conflict that has to be hand-resolved — which is where the real
# damage came from, since a hand-resolve once renumbered the OTHER session's
# already-merged entries.
#
# ⚑ This trades a merge conflict for a possible DUPLICATE sequence number, and
# that trade is only safe because `bun scripts/delta-lint.ts` is loud about
# duplicates in CI. A duplicate is not cosmetic: the flogence bridge uses the
# sequence as a checkpoint cursor, so the second entry to merge reads as
# already-absorbed and drops out of the digest. The two changes land together;
# neither is sufficient alone.
handOffs/delta-log.md merge=union
